      {
        "id": "lem-cm-matrix-curve-derivative-rules",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Derivative rules for differentiable matrix-valued curves, and skewness of $R^{\\mathsf T}R'$ for a curve in $SO(3)$",
        "statement": "For A,B:I->M_3(R) differentiable at t0: (A+B)'=A'+B', (A^T)'=(A')^T, (AB)'=A'B+AB'; and if A(t) in SO(3) throughout, then A^T A' and A' A^T are skew-symmetric at t0.",
        "deps": [
          "def-derivative",
          "thm-algebra-of-derivatives",
