      {
        "id": "lem-cm-mass-moments-are-finite",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Finiteness of the moments of a bounded finite Borel measure on $\\mathbb R^3$",
        "statement": "Assume AC_omega. For a bounded finite Borel measure nu with nu(R^3 \\ B_R(0))=0: the coordinate functions and their pairwise products are Borel measurable and nu-integrable with int|rho_j|dnu <= R nu(R^3) and int|rho_j rho_k|dnu <= R^2 nu(R^3); hence the total mass, first moment and inertia entries are well-defined finite reals with |mu_j|<=R nu(R^3) and |I_jk|<=2R^2 nu(R^3).",
        "deps": [
          "def-cm-mass-distribution-and-inertia-matrix",
          "def-countable-choice",
