      {
        "id": "def-cm-rigid-placement-and-body-angular-velocity",
        "kind": "definition",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Rigid placements, body and spatial angular velocity, and material velocities",
        "statement": "For differentiable c:I->R^3 and R:I->SO(3), the rigid placement is x(t,rho)=c(t)+R(t)rho with material velocities dx/dt = c'(t)+R'(t)rho. Since R^T R' is skew, there is a unique body angular velocity omega with R^T R'=[omega]_x; the spatial angular velocity is R omega; if R is twice differentiable then omega is differentiable.",
        "deps": [
          "def-cm-mass-distribution-and-inertia-matrix",
