      {
        "id": "lem-cm-inertia-matrix-properties",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Symmetry, the quadratic identity $\\omega^{\\mathsf T}I\\omega=\\int\\lVert\\omega\\times\\rho\\rVert_2^2\\,d\\nu$, and the positive-definiteness criterion for the inertia matrix",
        "statement": "Under the Axiom of Countable Choice AC_omega, used only for finiteness of the entries of I: for a mass distribution with inertia matrix I: I is symmetric; omega^T I omega = int ||omega x rho||^2 dnu >= 0 for every omega; I is positive definite exactly when {rho: omega x rho = 0} is nu-null for every omega != 0; and if I is positive definite then I is invertible.",
        "deps": [
