      {
        "id": "thm-cm-rigid-kinetic-energy-and-angular-momentum",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Kinetic energy and angular momentum of a rigid placement: $K=\\tfrac12m\\lVert c'\\rVert_2^2+\\tfrac12\\omega^{\\mathsf T}I\\omega$ and $L_c=RI\\omega$",
        "statement": "Under the Axiom of Countable Choice AC_omega, used only for integrability of the two integrands: for a centred mass distribution and a rigid placement: dx/dt(t,rho)=c'(t)+R(t)(omega(t) x rho) and R'=R[omega]_x=[R omega]_x R; the kinetic energy and angular momentum about c (defined as the corresponding componentwise integrals) are finite and satisfy K(t)=1/2 m||c'(t)||^2+1/2 omega(t)^T I omega(t) and L_c(t)=R(t) I omega(t).",
        "deps": [
          "def-cm-rigid-placement-and-body-angular-velocity",
          "def-cm-mass-distribution-and-inertia-matrix",
