      {
        "id": "cor-cm-principal-axes-of-the-inertia-matrix",
        "kind": "corollary",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Principal axes and principal moments of the inertia matrix, and positivity in the nondegenerate case",
        "statement": "The inertia matrix has an orthonormal eigenbasis (e_1,e_2,e_3) with real eigenvalues I_j (principal axes and moments); in that basis I omega = sum I_j omega_j e_j and omega^T I omega = sum I_j omega_j^2 = int ||omega x rho||^2 dnu >= 0. Each I_j vanishes exactly when {rho: e_j x rho=0} is nu-null; if the inertia form is positive definite then all I_j>0 and I is invertible with I^{-1}e_j=I_j^{-1}e_j; if nu is supported on no line through the origin then all I_j>0.",
        "deps": [
          "def-cm-mass-distribution-and-inertia-matrix",
          "lem-cm-inertia-matrix-properties",
          "cor-real-spectral-theorem-for-self-adjoint-endomorphisms",
          "def-self-adjoint-and-normal-endomorphism",
          "prop-self-adjoint-and-normal-matrix-criteria-in-orthonormal-bases",
          "def-orthogonal-vectors-sets-and-orthonormal-bases",
          "def-euclidean-inner-product",
          "def-inner-product-space",
