        "id": "thm-cm-euler-equations-and-torque-free-invariants",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Euler's equations $I\\omega'+\\omega\\times I\\omega=R^{\\mathsf T}\\tau$ under an adopted torque balance, and the torque-free invariants and principal-axis equations",
        "statement": "Under the adopted balance hypothesis (R l)' = tau with l=I omega: Euler's equations I omega' + omega x I omega = R^T tau hold. If tau=0 then l'=l x (I^{-1} l), and ||l||^2 and 1/2 <l,I^{-1}l> are constant; in an orthonormal eigenbasis l_1'=(1/I_3-1/I_2)l_2l_3 and cyclically, with ||l||^2=sum l_j^2 and 1/2<l,I^{-1}l>=sum l_j^2/(2I_j) constant.",
