        "id": "def-cm-euler-angle-parametrization-and-heavy-top-system",
        "kind": "definition",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "The Euler-angle parametrization and the heavy symmetric top system",
        "statement": "The Euler-angle parametrization is Theta(phi,theta,psi)=R_z(phi)R_y(theta)R_z(psi) on R x (0,pi) x R, with no injectivity or chart property claimed; the heavy-top function is L=1/2 A(theta'^2+phi'^2 sin^2 theta)+1/2 C(psi'+phi' cos theta)^2 - m g d cos theta with explicit partial derivatives; a heavy-top trajectory is a C^2 curve satisfying the three displayed second-order equations d/dt(dL/dphi')=0, d/dt(dL/dtheta')=dL/dtheta, d/dt(dL/dpsi')=0.",
