        "id": "thm-cm-heavy-top-reduction",
        "kind": "theorem",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Reduction of the heavy symmetric top system: conserved momenta, one-dimensional $\\theta$ equation and conserved reduced energy",
        "statement": "Along any heavy-top trajectory: b=C(psi'+phi'cos theta) and a=A phi'sin^2 theta + b cos theta are constant; phi'=(a-b cos theta)/(A sin^2 theta) and psi'=b/C-(a-b cos theta)cos theta/(A sin^2 theta); the reduced energy 1/2 A theta'^2+(a-bcos theta)^2/(2A sin^2 theta)+b^2/(2C)+m g d cos theta is constant; and A theta'' = -U'(theta) for the effective potential U.",
        "deps": [
