        "id": "lem-cm-euler-angle-angular-velocity",
        "kind": "lemma",
        "domain": "mathematics",
        "title": "Angular velocity in Euler angles: $\\omega_3=\\psi'+\\varphi'\\cos\\theta$ and $\\omega_1^2+\\omega_2^2=\\theta'^2+\\varphi'^2\\sin^2\\theta$",
        "statement": "For R(t)=Theta(phi(t),theta(t),psi(t)) with theta in (0,pi), the body angular velocity is omega=(-phi'sin theta cos psi+theta' sin psi, phi'sin theta sin psi+theta' cos psi, psi'+phi'cos theta) in the standard basis; hence omega_3=psi'+phi'cos theta, omega_1^2+omega_2^2=theta'^2+phi'^2 sin^2 theta, and for the diagonal inertia with moments (A,A,C) one has omega^T I omega = A(theta'^2+phi'^2 sin^2 theta)+C(psi'+phi'cos theta)^2.",
