        "title": "Finite point-mass inertia matrices computed and checked against the positivity criterion",
        "statement": "Under the Axiom of Countable Choice AC_omega, used only for finiteness of the inertia entries: for finite weighted sums of Dirac measures, the inertia matrices are computed in three cases: two unit masses at +-e_3 give I=diag(2,2,0); three unit masses at an equilateral triangle in the plane e_3=0 give I=diag(3/2,3/2,3); two unit masses at e_1 and 2e_1 give I=diag(0,5,5) with nonzero first moment. Each case is checked against the quadratic identity and the positive-definiteness criterion.",
