        "title": "Finite checks of the torque-free spin results: stability certificates, an escape-time bound, and the linearized dichotomy",
        "statement": "For (I_1,I_2,I_3)=(1,2,3): the stability certificates are c=1/4 and c_3=1/12, with the explicit certificate bound l_1^2+l_2^2<=1/25 about e_3; the intermediate-axis escape data are a=sqrt3, delta_0=1/4, c_0=1/4, epsilon_0=1/2 with escape time bound 4 log 25 for eta=1/100; and the linearized formulas are checked in both the oscillatory case (Omega=2, lambda=-4) and the exponential case ((I_1,I_2,I_3)=(1,3,2), lambda=4/3).",
